<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila raises 91-day special series T-bill rate.</title>
<headline>Manila raises 91-day special series T-bill rate.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Central Bank on Tuesday raised rates on its 91-day special series treasury bills to 10.356 percent from 10.10 percent.</p>
<p>The rate was raised to align it with the results of the T-bills auction on Monday.</p>
<p>The bank also made new offerings for 182 days, quoting a rate of 10.597 percent and 364 days with a rate of 11.088 percent.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8934</p>
